  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At OHLA, Luis Amodio emphasised examining projects before committing to build them. A selection committee assessed the viability of each proposed job, making financial scrutiny part of the bidding process. Managing interests across the Atlantic also shaped his routine: he divided his working time between Spain and Mexico, remaining in contact across their different time zones.\n\nHis approach to property development also distinguished between scale and returns. He questioned projects that absorbed large sums over long construction periods, and explored student accommodation and tourist housing as alternatives. Around Málaga, he identified opportunities for these more focused forms of development.",
    "html": "<p>At OHLA, Luis Amodio emphasised examining projects before committing to build them. A selection committee assessed the viability of each proposed job, making financial scrutiny part of the bidding process. Managing interests across the Atlantic also shaped his routine: he divided his working time between Spain and Mexico, remaining in contact across their different time zones.</p>\r\n<p>His approach to property development also distinguished between scale and returns. He questioned projects that absorbed large sums over long construction periods, and explored student accommodation and tourist housing as alternatives. Around Málaga, he identified opportunities for these more focused forms of development.</p>\r\n",
